From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 18:39:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 203/208] avcodec/vc1: read RESPIC only in I and P pictures

RESPIC is present in Simple and Main profile I and P pictures only
(SMPTE 421M 7.1.1.23, and the SMPTE reference decoder); B and BI
pictures keep the value of the last I or P picture. The B check missed
BI pictures, which are signalled as B pictures with BFRACTION = 0 and
have been turned into AV_PICTURE_TYPE_BI by then, so 2 bits too many
were read from the header of every BI picture of a MULTIRES sequence.

Signed-off-by: Jernej Skrabec <jernej.skrabec@siol.net>
---
 libavcodec/vc1.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libavcodec/vc1.c b/libavcodec/vc1.c
index e365aaec84..b50a05e274 100644
--- a/libavcodec/vc1.c
+++ b/libavcodec/vc1.c
@@ -695,7 +695,8 @@ int ff_vc1_parse_frame_header(VC1Context *v, GetBitContext* gb)
     v->k_y = v->mvrange + 8; //k_y can be 8 9 10 11
     v->range_x = 1 << (v->k_x - 1);
     v->range_y = 1 << (v->k_y - 1);
-    if (v->multires && v->s.pict_type != AV_PICTURE_TYPE_B)
+    if (v->multires && (v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I ||
+                        v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_P))
         v->respic = get_bits(gb, 2);
 
     if (v->res_x8 && (v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_I || v->s.pict_type == AV_PICTURE_TYPE_BI)) {
